 ## Sharing a VM
 
 The full app and an embedding app open the same VM in the default folder ([finding the VM](#finding-the-vm)), never at once: the VM folder's lock refuses the second. The run mode reports `vm-already-open`, and the full app says that Omarchy is open in another app, such as Omarchy Installer. Either can boot a VM the other made. The `try-omarchy` package only upgrades, so an older kit never downgrades the guest. A launcher refuses a VM whose `vm.json` names a storage layout it does not know (`storage-layout-unknown`).
+
+### Focused clipboard routing (private POC patch)
+
+The native clipboard bridge reads and writes the Mac clipboard only while its exact QEMU process is frontmost and its captured kernel process identity is still alive. Unknown focus fails closed. It needs no additional Accessibility grant. Focus gain synchronizes the current Mac clipboard once; a background guest's clipboard and sync messages are ignored. A quarter-second poll reconciles focus, and each clipboard side effect checks focus again on the bridge's serial state queue. Echo markers reset at observed focus loss/gain. If a guest message first observes focus gain, the current host selection wins that transition.
+
+The global Mac clipboard still transfers content intentionally when the user switches guests. The change prevents background broadcast and background writes; it does not create private host clipboards. The client configuration and run protocol remain at version 1. Deterministic two-route tests cover shared pasteboard isolation, rapid activation, focus loss during reads and immediately before side effects. Real two-guest focus behaviour remains to be validated on Apple Silicon.
diff --git a/macos/Sources/OmarchyVMHelper/NativeClipboardBridge.swift b/macos/Sources/OmarchyVMHelper/NativeClipboardBridge.swift
index 39b07ba..77f297f 100644
--- a/macos/Sources/OmarchyVMHelper/NativeClipboardBridge.swift
+++ b/macos/Sources/OmarchyVMHelper/NativeClipboardBridge.swift
@@ -197,29 +197,123 @@ final class GeneralPasteboard: HostPasteboardProviding {
     }
 }
 
+protocol ClipboardFocusProviding: AnyObject {
+    func isFocused() -> Bool
+}
+
+final class QEMUClipboardFocus: ClipboardFocusProviding {
+    private let processIdentity: KernelProcessIdentity
+
+    init(processIdentity: KernelProcessIdentity) {
+        self.processIdentity = processIdentity
+    }
+
+    func isFocused() -> Bool {
+        processIdentity.isStillRunning &&
+            NSWorkspace.shared.frontmostApplication?.processIdentifier == processIdentity.processIdentifier
+    }
+}
+
+final class FocusedClipboardRouting {
+    private let pasteboard: HostPasteboardProviding
+    private let focus: ClipboardFocusProviding
+    private let send: (Data) throws -> Void
+    private var state = ClipboardSyncState()
+    private var wasFocused = false
+    private var observedChangeCount: Int?
+
+    init(pasteboard: HostPasteboardProviding, focus: ClipboardFocusProviding,
+         send: @escaping (Data) throws -> Void) {
+        self.pasteboard = pasteboard
+        self.focus = focus
+        self.send = send
+    }
+
+    private func stillFocused() -> Bool {
+        guard focus.isFocused() else {
+            wasFocused = false
+            observedChangeCount = nil
+            state = ClipboardSyncState()
+            return false
+        }
+        return true
+    }
+
+    private func reconcileFocus() throws -> (focused: Bool, gained: Bool) {
+        guard stillFocused() else { return (false, false) }
+        let gained = !wasFocused
+        wasFocused = true
+        if gained {
+            state = ClipboardSyncState()
+            try sendHostSelection()
+        }
+        return (wasFocused, gained)
+    }
+
+    private func sendHostSelection() throws {
+        guard stillFocused() else { return }
+        let count = pasteboard.changeCount
+        let message = pasteboard.read()
+        guard stillFocused() else { return }
+        observedChangeCount = count
+        guard let message, state.hostChanged(message) else { return }
+        let data = try message.encode()
+        guard stillFocused() else { return }
+        try send(data)
+    }
+
+    func poll() throws {
+        let transition = try reconcileFocus()
+        guard transition.focused, !transition.gained else { return }
+        guard stillFocused(), pasteboard.changeCount != observedChangeCount else { return }
+        try sendHostSelection()
+    }
+
+    func handle(_ line: ClipboardMessage.GuestLine) throws {
+        let transition = try reconcileFocus()
+        guard transition.focused else { return }
+        switch line {
+        case .sync:
+            guard !transition.gained else { return }
+            state = ClipboardSyncState()
+            try sendHostSelection()
+        case .clipboard(let message):
+            guard !transition.gained, stillFocused(), state.guestChanged(message) else { return }
+            guard stillFocused() else { return }
+            pasteboard.write(message)
+            observedChangeCount = pasteboard.changeCount
+        case .ignored:
+            return
+        }
+    }
+}
+
